Z||000020||2M4 Dale||10-03-1999||06:17 PM||||Whats the diference between notchback and fastback scoop? My car is a notchback. Also does the scoop effect proper heat evacuation from the engine compartment? One more dumb question...How do you open the hood with the scoop in place? Does it have to come off or what?||||reg||1
Z||000021||88 Fiero||10-03-1999||07:10 PM||||The difference between the Fastback deck lid and the Notchback is that the Fastbacks have a higher position of the deck lid vs. the notchback which has a lower position of the deck lid. Also, the '84 Fiero deck lid is different than the '85 to '88. The difference is that on the '84 it's flat with louvers and the '85 to '88 has a hump on the lid...The purpose of the Over the Roof Scoop on the Fiero's back on IMSA Racing is to draw more air to it's throttle body or carburated body...as far as cooling the engine...I don't think it will help...When the club went to the Pontiac Assembly Plant for Fiero's the question we ask them is how do air circulate in the engine compartment.. We were told that the air flows under the car and goes over the  the top of the engine and exit on the other side of the engine...pretty weird flow...Darn forgot your last question...The way the Scoop mounted on the deck lid is that it has a plate screw on the deck lid and a piston that attaches to the Scoop and the other end to the plate.. When you want to open the deck lid. You tilt up the Scoop and raise your deck lid....<P>[This message has been edited by 88 Fiero (edited 10-03-1999).]<p>[This message has been edited by 88 Fiero (edited 10-03-1999).]||||reg||1
